title: After setup, "Now you can use it" sends the reader to a reference that opens on refused saves, and no page says how to make a first note.
pid: 30dc2820-88fc-4a96-9999-62421f653332
body: |2-
  'COMMANDS.org' spends its first ninety lines on conflicts between
  views, baselines, recovering a refused save, Hoist, overPrivateText
  telescopes and "skgsave-committed": none of it met before. That a
  note is a headline, that C-c v e opens an empty view to write one
  in, and that a save asks which skgrepo a new root goes in, no page
  puts together; C-c v e sits under "view changes, global", and its
  "why" speaks of ghosts, tombstones and unknown viewnodes. What the
  client shows just after it starts I could not tell. A first link is
  findable once one knows search is 'C-c f': C-c f l, search then link,
  is plain.
  Change: a short page, "your first ten minutes", linked from that line
  of setup: a small ordinary tree drawn (the dentist of
  'data-model_friendly.org' would do (d)), and the keys that make,
  save, find, open and link it: C-c v e, C-x C-s, C-c f RET,
  C-c g RET, C-c f l. Then 'COMMANDS.org' for the rest.
